  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "With default quality settings in open beta shadow quality for realtime directional light shadows has taken a nosedive. Shadow quality in Unity is already unacceptably bad and shadow quality just gets way worse in open beta.\nAlbum with comparisons: https://imgur.com/a/k5EIYvv\nThe issue is that all quality settings that are not ultra have their shadow cascade count set at 2. This is especially an issue that the default quality level does this since it's effectively an automatic downgrade to all content and will cause complaints to world, avatar, and shadow authors over the new default. If the shadow cascades get lowered to 2, it should only be done on the Low quality setting or *maybe* medium imo.\nLowering shadow cascades has many issues for existing content. Primarily it increases light leaking significantly, where you will see light behind objects that are supposed to cast a shadow. It obviously lowers shadow quality very noticeably which turns most shadows into formless blobs. On avatars shadows were already terrible to the point that people turn off shadow casting on their avatars to avoid self shadowing. This only makes it even worse and removes what little bit of shadow resolution was left on players. Due to the lowered resolution when things move in shadows, their shadowed parts flicker much more than before as well.",
